==Weaknesses==
<gallery type="slideshow">
Hunted (579).png|Neutralized Intangibility/Invisibility
Hunted (541).png|Trackable Heat
AND (116).png|Ineffective Body Possession
VM (508).png|Body Possession Rejection
CS (446).png|Electricity Vulnerability
</gallery>
If Ghostfreak's protoplasm is solidified, he will be unable to turn intangible or invisible. Certain substances can solidify Ghostfreak's protoplasm, such as a special orange liquid used by [[Kraab (Classic)|Kraab]].<ref name="Hunted" /> It is possible that [[Gutrot]]'s [[Gutrot's Species|species]] can replicate this liquid in a gaseous form.{{Refn|[[:File:Gutrot Can Replicate Kraab's Liquid.png]]|group = DJW}}

Ghostfreak's intangibility requires conscious thought to activate, so opponents will be able to hit him if he is caught off-guard, as seen when he got hit by a punching bag that [[Thumbskull (Classic)|Thumbskull]] threw at him while he was distracted.<ref name="GO" /> 

There are a number of weaknesses that Ghostfreak is vulnerable to if he remains tangible and caught off-guard. For example: 
*He can be harmed by electricity, such as that generated by [[Transylian]]s<ref name="BAotD" /> [[Conductoid]]s,<ref name="RMP" /> and by [[Charmcaster (Classic)|Charmcaster]].<ref name="CS" /> The former two were demonstrated with Zs'Skayr.
*He can be controlled by [[Vladat]]s via their [[Corruptura]]s, as demonstrated by many Ectonurite residents of [[Anur Transyl]].<ref name="TVSB" />

Ghostfreak can be tracked by opponents who can sense heat or use thermographic vision, as demonstrated by Kraab.<ref name="Hunted" />

There are certain beings Ghostfreak cannot possess. For example, he cannot possess zombies due to them lacking minds of their own.<ref name="AND">''[[A New Dawn]]''</ref> He is also not able to possess [[Omnitrix]] transformations,<ref name="GO" /> including the [[Ultimate Forms#Sentient Forms|Sentient Ultimate forms]] (when inside the [[Ultimatrix (Original)|Ultimatrix]]);<ref name="TUS" /> nor [[Dagon]].{{Refn|[[:File:Ectonurites Cannot Possess Dagon.png]]|group = DJW}}

Even if Ghostfreak does possess someone, it may be possible for them to reject him out of their body, as shown with [[Ma Vreedle]].<ref>''[[Vreedlemania]]''</ref>

Like the rest of his kind, Ghostfreak cannot survive on [[Anur Vladias]].{{Refn|[[:File:What Anur Vladias used to be like.png]]|group = DJW}}

Ghostfreak can be scared by [[Toepick]]'s [[Toepick's Species|species]].{{Refn|[[:File:Toepick Can Scare Ectonurites.png]]|group = DJW}}

Ghostfreak can be affected by a [[Nemuina]]'s sleeping dust.{{Refn|[[:File:Pesky Dust Works On Chronosapiens and Ectonurites.png]]|group = DJW}}

==History==
===1773=== 
*In ''[[A New Dawn]]'', 16-year-old [[Ben Tennyson (Classic)|Ben]] as Ghostfreak failed to possess the zombie [[Red Coat]].

===Prior to Ben 10=== 
*[[Myaxx]] unknowingly added Ghostfreak's [[Ectonurite (Classic)|Ectonurite]] DNA to the [[Omnitrix (Original)|Omnitrix]] when she did not realize [[Zs'Skayr]] possessed the [[Florauna (Classic)|Florauna]] that was being sampled for [[Wildvine (Classic)|Wildvine]]'s DNA.{{Refn|group = pop-up|name = Florauna}}<ref name="BAotD" />

===Ben 10===   
*Ghostfreak first appeared in ''[[Permanent Retirement]]'', where he frightened [[Gwen Tennyson (Classic)|Gwen]], escaped [[Vera Tennyson|Vera]]'s house, drove a golf cart, was about to steal an apple pie before being disgusted by a [[Limax]] disguised as a [[Human (Classic)|human]] woman, and then followed another one disguised as [[Marty]].
*In ''[[Hunted]]'', Ghostfreak failed to scare Gwen and defeated [[Kraab (Classic)|Kraab]].
*In ''[[Last Laugh]]'', Ghostfreak scared and defeated [[Zombozo (Classic)|Zombozo]], freeing everyone's happiness in the process.
*In ''[[Kevin 11 (Episode)|Kevin 11]]'', Ghostfreak snuck into a game room and played a '''[[Sumo Slammers (Classic)|Sumo Slammers]]''' video game.
*In ''[[Secrets]]'', Ghostfreak briefly appeared in the middle of a fight before the malfunctioning [[Omnitrix (Original)|Omnitrix]] made him switch into [[Grey Matter (Classic)|Grey Matter]]. Later, Ghostfreak escaped from [[Vilgax (Classic)|Vilgax]] and searched for Gwen and [[Max Tennyson (Classic)|Max]] before switching into [[Wildmutt]].
**Also, Ghostfreak appeared as one of the many alien templates used for Vilgax's army in an imaginary sequence.
*In ''[[The Big Tick]]'', Ghostfreak failed to defeat the [[Great One]].
*In ''[[Framed]]'', Gwen mentioned Ghostfreak was used by [[Kevin Levin (Classic)|Kevin]] to terrorize Barstow, California.
*At some point prior to ''[[Ghostfreaked Out]]'', Ghostfreak snuck into a horror movie, during which Zs'Skayr secretly took control and contacted [[Dr. Viktor]] with his plans.{{Refn|group = pop-up|name = movie}}<ref name="BAotD" />
*In ''[[Ghostfreaked Out]]'', Ghostfreak tricked and tortured [[Wildmutt]] in a dream. Later, Zs'Skayr took over Ghostfreak and violently battled the [[Circus Freaks (Classic)|Circus Freaks]] until he reverted.
**This would remove Ghostfreak from the active playlist, thereby allowing Zs'Skayr to escape the Omnitrix.
*In ''[[Be Afraid of the Dark]]'', Ben regained Ghostfreak (in his true form) by unknowingly scanning Zs'Skayr, though Ben never transforms into Ghostfreak for the remainder of the series out of fear the evil Ectonurite would take over again.

===Prior to Alien Force===   
*At some point in time, Ghostfreak was removed from the Omnitrix.

===Alien Force===   
*In ''[[Ghost Town]]'', [[Ben Tennyson (Classic)|Ben]] scanned Zs'Skayr again and transformed into Ghostfreak. When Zs'Skayr quickly regained control, Ghostfreak was able to revert to Ben with the "help" of [[Vilgax (Classic)|Vilgax]].

===Ultimate Alien===  
*In ''[[The Ultimate Sacrifice]]'', Ghostfreak escaped [[Sentient Ultimate Spidermonkey]]'s webbing and failed to possess [[Sentient Ultimate Humungousaur]] before being frozen by [[Sentient Ultimate Big Chill]], forcing him to switch into [[Heatblast (Classic)|Heatblast]].

===Omniverse===  
*In ''[[Mystery, Incorporeal]]'', Ghostfreak saved [[Helena Xagliv|Professor Xagliv]] from [[Michael Morningstar (Classic)|Michael Morningstar]], then possessed the latter and made him stop the [[Spells (Classic)|spell]] in order to save [[Gwen Tennyson (Classic)|Gwen]]. 
**From this moment on, [[Ben Tennyson (Classic)|Ben]] has overcome his apprehension of using Ghostfreak since the persona of Zs'Skayr is no longer present.
*In ''[[Bengeance is Mine]]'', Ghostfreak battled [[Psyphon]] and saved a busload of people.
*In ''[[Charm School]]'', Ghostfreak searched for [[Charmcaster (Classic)|Charmcaster]] in [[Friedkin University]] and lured her into the library before she defeated him.
*In ''[[Vreedlemania]]'', Ghostfreak possessed [[Ma Vreedle]] and ordered the [[Pretty_Boy_Clones|Pretty Boys]] to stop wreaking havoc on [[Bellwood (Classic)|Bellwood]] until Ma fought him out of her body once the Vreedles deduced it was not really her speaking.
*In ''[[Malgax Attacks]]'', Ghostfreak defeated some of [[Vilgax (Classic)|Vilgax]]'s [[Mechadroid|Mechadroids]].
*In ''[[A New Dawn]]'', Ghostfreak battled a zombie and later appeared for a short time when Ben was cycling through his aliens.

===Bad Ben's Timeline=== 
*In ''[[And Then There Were None]]'', [[Bad Ben|Bad]] Ghostfreak chased after [[Ben Tennyson (No Watch Timeline)|No Watch Ben]].

