==Trivia==
*According to himself in the '''[[Ben 10 (2005 TV Series)|Original Series]]''', [[Ben Tennyson (Classic)|Ben]] was always creeped out when he was Ghostfreak. Even six years later (especially after the [[Zs'Skayr]] incident), he was still afraid to transform into him. When he transforms into Ghostfreak in ''[[Mystery, Incorporeal]]'', he states that he feels like himself, suggesting that Ghostfreak now exists independently from Zs'Skayr. 
**As such, in the '''Original Series''', Ghostfreak was the least used out of all the original ten aliens Ben had access to, only appearing in seven episodes and being used a total of nine times.
*In ''[[The Alliance]]'', Ben wanted to use Ghostfreak to try and help an injured [[Max Tennyson (Classic)|Max]] at the hospital by "melding" with him. This indicates that Ben already knew about Ghostfreak's ability to possess people, even though he never does this onscreen until ''Ghostfreaked Out''.
*Despite using him at least once to terrorize a city when he was 11,<ref>[[Gwen Tennyson (Classic)|Gwen Tennyson]]</ref><ref>''[[Framed]]''</ref> [[Kevin Levin (Classic)|Kevin]] states he never liked Ghostfreak.<ref>''[[Save the Last Dance]]''</ref> This was likely due to feeling Zs'Skayr's presence while as [[Kevin 11]].{{Refn|[[:File:Kevin 11 Contains Zs'Skayr.png]]|group = DR}}
*Ghostfreak is one of five aliens to appear in each series of the Classic Continuity; the other four being [[Cannonbolt (Classic)|Cannonbolt]], [[Upchuck]], [[Way Big (Classic)|Way Big]], and [[Diamondhead (Classic)|Diamondhead]].
**However, Ghostfreak is the only one of these aliens who has changed his appearance throughout all four series of the Classic Continuity, albeit it was only due to using his true form in '''[[Ben 10: Alien Force (TV Series)|Alien Force]]''' and outermost-skinned form in '''[[Ben 10: Ultimate Alien (TV Series)|Ultimate Alien]]'''.
*Ghostfreak is also one of the only five aliens who escaped from the [[Omnitrix (Original)|original Omnitrix]]; the others being [[Chromastone (Classic)|Chromastone]], [[Spidermonkey (Classic)|Spidermonkey]], [[Goop (Classic)|Goop]], and Way Big.
**However, he is the only one to do it out of his own volition.
*In the [[Ben 10 (2005 TV Series)/Theme Song|intro]] for the first two seasons of the '''Original Series''', Ghostfreak's eye is red instead of purple.  
**It is also worth noting that after Season 2, when Zs'Skayr successfully escapes the Omnitrix and thus removing Ghostfreak from it, he is replaced with Cannonbolt in the intro for the third and fourth seasons.
*[[Duncan Rouleau|Duncan Roleau]] believes that Ghostfreak is one of few exceptions to the principle that transformations are not full-blown aliens due to retaining Ben's personality, memories, and consciousness;  other one being [[Feedback]].{{Refn|[[:File:Alien DNA Injected.PNG]]|group = DR}}{{Refn|[[:File:Most Aliens Aren't Full Aliens.png]]|group = DR}}
*Ghostfreak is a living being; the [[Ectonurite (Classic)|Ectonurite]] concept of "life" is just very different from most sentient life forms.{{Refn|name = Derrick|group = DJW}}
*If the Omnitrix times out while Ghostfreak is possessing something, Ben would pop out before becoming solid.{{Refn|[[:File:Ghostfreak Possession Time Out.png]]|group = DJW}}
*As of '''Ultimate Alien''', Ben has learned how to retract his outermost layer of skin as Ghostfreak.{{Refn|[[:File:Ben Has Learned To Retract Ghostfreak's Skin.png]]|group = DM}}
*When Ghostfreak was taunting [[Kraab (Classic)|Kraab]] in ''[[Hunted]]'', Ben may not have been the one in control.{{Refn|[[:File:Not Real Ben Talking.png]]|group = pop-up}}<ref name="Hunted" /> After he reverted, Ben even stated that it felt "even weirder" than when he is normally Ghostfreak.
*Ghostfreak is the first alien form that has managed to repress Ben's personality. [[Eon (Transformation)|Eon]] followed this trend prior to being retconned.{{Refn|[[:File:Eon Repress Ben's Personality.png]]|group = pop-up}}<ref>'''''[[Ben 10: Race Against Time]]'''''</ref>
*Ghostfreak was first envisioned by [[Ben 10 (2005 TV Series)/Early Development#Ghostfreak|Steve E. Gordon]] as an humanoid with dark blue suit, orange cape, gloves and mask with hair-like tendrills. [[Dave Johnson]] designed Ghostfreak for the '''Original Series'''. Looking back on the design, he noted he found the eye quite funny.{{Refn|https://archive.is/qKNnY|group = DJ}}
*Ghostfreak's green-tinted skin in '''[[Ben 10: Omniverse (TV Series)|Omniverse]]''' was inspired by the coloration of glow-in-the-dark toys.{{Refn|[[:File:OV ghostfreak inspiration.PNG]]|group = DJW}}
*"[[Ben Tennyson (Classic)|Ben's]] not here", a line said by Ghostfreak in ''[[Ghostfreaked Out]]'', was used in auditions for the role.{{Refn|''[[Ghostfreaked Out]]''; [https://preservetube.com/watch?v&#61;x_lycH63x3s link]|group = AC}}
*Had he appeared in '''Omniverse''' flashbacks, 11-year-old Ghostfreak would not have the chains.{{Refn|[[:File:OV Young Ghostfreak.png]]|group = DJW}}
**[[Derrick J. Wyatt]] eventually drew 11-year-old Ghostfreak as part of a GoFundMe in 2020.{{Refn|https://www.gofundme.com/f/derrick-j-wyatt-draws-ov-fasttrack--more|group = DJW}}
*In a [https://4.bp.blogspot.com/-AkeV_2wG8JQ/W7ELJRXrsmI/AAAAAAAAyhw/NewbPeHx2n4uWQsOA12ANx0VA53pxp6awCLcBGAs/s1600/Ben%2B10%2BHalloween%2B2018%2B-%2BBen%2B10%2BExtranet.jpg promotional image] for [[Cartoon Network]] and Ayala Mall's Animate Your Life This Halloween, [[Ben Tennyson (Reboot)|Reboot Ben]] is seen wearing a Ghostfreak costume.
*Had Ghostfreak appeared in the [[Ben 10 (2016 TV Series)|Reboot]], his design would have been similar to his appearance in the '''Original Series''' with the [[Omnitrix (Reboot)|Omnitrix]] symbol peeking out from under his outermost skin.{{Refn|[[:File:Hypothetical RB Ghostfreak.png]]|group = DR}}
*Ghostfreak is one of [[Duncan Rouleau]]'s favorite Omnitrix alien.{{Refn|https://youtu.be/IzdAJuPoKnU|group = DR}}

